{#
  Persistent top nav — shared by the board and every second page.

  `nav_root` is "" on the board and "../" on a profile page, so the same
  links resolve from either depth. `nav_here` marks the current page so
  its link reads as active.

  The theme switch is included here too, so it is on every page and only
  defined once. Its JS lives in _nav_script.
#}
<header class="sitenav">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="{{ nav_root }}index.html">
      <span class="brand-mark">⚓</span>
      <span class="brand-name">{{ guild_name }}</span>
    </a>
    {# Consolidated 2026-07-23: five thin tabs -> three top-level entries.
       Voyage and The Hall/Trophies fold into ship rooms (docs/STATUS.md
       "Navigation IA") rather than staying separate top-nav pages; Wanted
       keeps a direct top-level door in addition to living in the Bar room,
       per SHIP_EXPERIENCE_VISION.md #1 ("two doors to the same room").

       "The Ship" points at index.html, not ship.html: build_trial.py
       deploys the ship.html.j2 render AS index.html (the entry point),
       so ship.html never exists in the shipped bundle
       (docs/INTEGRATION_PLAN.md #1 — this was leaving ../ship.html
       dangling on every profile/secondary page).

       Clean Data now has a real destination: /review/clean-data/
       (docs/INTEGRATION_PLAN.md #2, 2026-07-23) — gated the same as the
       rest of /review, so linking it here adds no new exposure. #}
    <nav class="navlinks" aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="{{ nav_root }}index.html"
         {% if nav_here == 'board' or nav_here == 'ship' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>The Ship</a>
      <a href="{{ nav_root }}wanted.html"
         {% if nav_here == 'wanted' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Wanted Board</a>
      <a href="{{ nav_root }}review/clean-data/">Clean&nbsp;Data</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="themeswitch" role="group" aria-label="Theme">
      {%- for key, t in themes.items() %}
      <button type="button" data-theme="{{ key }}"
              aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if key == default_theme else 'false' }}"
              title="{{ t.label }}">{{ t.label }}</button>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
{%- if nav_here != 'board' %}
{# a big, obvious return affordance — the thing Zach could not find #}
<a class="backbar" href="{{ nav_root }}index.html">← Back to the ship</a>
{%- endif %}
